{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>If a man is found stealing a person.</b> Why is this said? Since it is stated below, ״וגונב איש״ etc. — I might hear even a son of eight years in the meaning. Therefore it says <b>מאחיו</b> — he is not liable unless he steals one who is viable." "<b>From his brother, of the children of Israel.</b> It further adds 'of the children of Israel' to exclude Esav, who is called 'brother.' The punishment we have heard; the warning, from where? It says <b>לא תגנב</b>."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 24, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:54:03.627275487Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}